# sys-flash: Wayward Cave 1F is DARK_FLASH. Flash from the party menu
# (FIELD_MOVES 15: do_flash_func + 0C3) sets FLAG_FLASH_ACTIVE and CLEAR. A warp to a cave (B1F and back)
# keeps it, so 1F stays CLEAR (decomp FieldMapChange_UpdateGameData); the warp outside clears it. The
# `dark`/`flash` screenshot lines mark the browser spec's darkness-radius check.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_BIBAREL 30 platinum:MOVE_FLASH
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_WAYWARD_CAVE_1F 30 54 left
until idle
+0 assert state weather "platinum:OVERWORLD_WEATHER_DARK_FLASH"
+0 screenshot dark
+0 field move 0 platinum:MOVE_FLASH
advance text
until idle
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_FLASH_ACTIVE true
+0 assert state weather "platinum:OVERWORLD_WEATHER_CLEAR"
+0 screenshot flash
# west to the stairs (28, 54) down to B1F, and back up the B1F stairs (16, 40)
+0 press left
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_WAYWARD_CAVE_B1F"
+0 release left
until idle
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_FLASH_ACTIVE true
+0 press right
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_WAYWARD_CAVE_1F"
+0 release right
until idle
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_FLASH_ACTIVE true
+0 assert state weather "platinum:OVERWORLD_WEATHER_CLEAR"
# out through the south exit (30, 55) to Route 206: not a cave, Flash ends
+0 press right
until position 30 54
+0 release right
+0 press down
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_206"
+0 release down
until idle
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_FLASH_ACTIVE false
